Purpose: Delete every remaining Windows and macOS branch in the bundled source trees (Plan 0003, Section 5.5). Windows path translation helpers collapse to the identity function, the macOS managed-preferences (MDM plist) machinery and its merge step are deleted, zip extraction loses its PowerShell path, the clipboard keeps its Linux and OSC 52 paths only, and the long tail of platform ternaries (suffixes, pagers, browser openers, process killing, watcher backends, protected-path tables, spawn options) is simplified to the Linux/Android form. After this patch, a search of packages/opencode/src, packages/core/src, and packages/tui/src for win32, darwin, powershell, pwsh, and cmd.exe returns no hits. The config test file loses the tests of the deleted managed-plist parser.
